+const termsSections=[
+ ['about','1. What these Terms cover',`<p>These Terms apply when you use NexMarkets to browse Debuts, get or hold a Pass, use an Advantage, list or buy a Pass in the Market, create an Edition, or use the Dashboard.</p><p>They are written to be readable because the rules matter more when people can understand them. A particular Edition can also have its own published terms. Those Edition terms control the specific product, Advantage, supply and other Edition details. These platform Terms control your use of NexMarkets itself.</p>`],
+ ['eligibility','2. Using NexMarkets',`<p>You are responsible for making sure you are allowed to use NexMarkets and enter the transactions you choose. Do not use the product to break the law, mislead another user, impersonate someone else, manipulate Market activity, or interfere with the service.</p><p>You are also responsible for the wallet you connect. Keep your private keys and seed phrase private. NexMarkets will never need your seed phrase to display or manage a Pass.</p>`],
+ ['passes','3. Passes, Editions and Debuts',`<p>A Debut is the initial release of a limited Edition. A Pass is one exact item from that Edition. Each Pass has its own serial and can carry an Advantage.</p><p>A Pass does not automatically represent equity, debt, a share of Builder revenue, ownership of the Builder business, ownership of product code, or intellectual property rights. If an Edition grants any specific right beyond the stated Advantage, that right must be written clearly in that Edition terms.</p>`],
+ ['advantages','4. Advantages',`<p>An Advantage is the holder benefit published for the Pass. The Builder is responsible for accurately describing the benefit and delivering the product or service side of the promise.</p><p>Some Advantages are connected automatically to a Builder product. Others are redeemed through NexMarkets. When an Advantage is partly used, the remaining state stays with the exact Pass. If the Pass is sold, the buyer receives what remains.</p><p>Advantage use is locked while a Pass is actively listed. This keeps the state a buyer sees from changing underneath an active listing.</p>`],
+ ['preview','5. Previews and Edition information',`<p>Builders publish a Preview before a Debut opens so people can inspect the product, Edition, Advantage and terms. The current Create flow requires a Preview period of at least 24 hours.</p><p>Builders should not hide material changes. NexMarkets can display a terms version and terms history so people can see when important information changed after the Preview became public.</p>`],
+ ['builders','6. Builder responsibilities',`<p>If you create a Debut, you are responsible for the accuracy of the product description, evidence, Edition information, Advantage, opening time, support information and terms you publish.</p><p>Do not publish an Advantage you cannot reasonably deliver. Do not use copied evidence, fake product claims, invented traction, misleading market information or another person's intellectual property without permission.</p><p>If you enable referral rewards, you are responsible for paying them. NexMarkets may keep the referral record, but the current referral flow is Builder settled.</p>`],
+ ['buyers','7. Holder and buyer responsibilities',`<p>Before buying, review the product, Advantage, Edition supply, price, network, current terms and the exact Pass state when buying from the Market.</p><p>You decide whether the purchase makes sense for you. NexMarkets does not promise that a Builder will succeed, that an Advantage will be valuable to you, that a Pass will rise in price, or that you will be able to sell it later.</p>`],
+ ['payments','8. Payment and transaction confirmation',`<p>The current Pass purchase flow uses USDG. The transaction surface shows the amount and network before confirmation.</p><p>Blockchain transactions can take time to confirm and can fail. A wallet confirmation does not always mean the final network state has settled. Do not repeatedly submit the same action until you know the earlier transaction failed.</p><p>After a blockchain transaction completes, it may not be reversible. Do not assume NexMarkets can cancel a settled purchase, restore a transferred Pass, or recover funds sent to the wrong address.</p>`],
+ ['fees','9. Fees and Builder Royalty',`<p>The current NexMarkets primary fee is <strong>5%</strong> of the amount collected through a Debut. The Create flow shows the fee and Builder amount before publication.</p><p>The current NexMarkets secondary fee is <strong>1%</strong> on a completed Market sale. A Builder can also choose a Builder Royalty from 0% to 5% for its Edition.</p><p>Builder Royalty is held for 30 days after a resale before it becomes available for withdrawal. This hold affects royalty withdrawal timing. It does not prevent the Pass itself from being bought or sold during that period.</p><p>Network gas and wallet provider costs are separate from NexMarkets fees and can vary.</p>`],
+ ['market','10. Market listings and resale',`<p>A listing is an offer by a holder to sell an exact Pass at an ask. It is not a guarantee that a sale will happen.</p><p>Market information such as floor, last sale, volume and chart history is provided as transaction context. It is not a promise of value, a forecast, or financial advice.</p><p>A listing can become invalid if ownership, Advantage state or another required condition changes. NexMarkets can reject or stop a stale or invalid listing instead of trying to complete it with old information.</p>`],
+ ['risk','11. Risk and no promise of profit',`<p>Products can fail. Builders can change direction. Advantages can become less useful to you. Markets can be inactive. A Pass can sell for less than you paid, or may not sell at all.</p><p>Do not treat a rising floor, a previous sale or a limited supply as a guarantee of future demand. NexMarkets gives you information to inspect an offer and an exact Pass. The decision remains yours.</p>`],
+ ['ip','12. Content and intellectual property',`<p>Builders keep responsibility for the content and rights they publish. Pass ownership does not transfer copyright, trademark rights, source code, product ownership or other intellectual property unless the specific Edition terms say so.</p><p>You may use NexMarkets interfaces and Pass exports for normal product use and sharing. You may not copy the service, misuse another person's content, or present someone else's Builder identity or Pass artwork as your own.</p>`],
+ ['availability','13. Service availability',`<p>NexMarkets depends on software, wallets, networks and external services that can be delayed or unavailable. We may need to pause a feature to protect users, repair a defect, handle a network issue or prevent an invalid transaction.</p><p>We will try to make state clear when something is pending, unavailable or failed. We do not promise uninterrupted access at every moment.</p>`],
+ ['changes','14. Changes to these Terms',`<p>These Terms can change as NexMarkets changes. When a material platform rule changes, the updated version and effective date should be published so users can read the current rules.</p><p>Edition terms are separate. A Builder changing its Edition terms should use the Edition terms history rather than silently replacing material information.</p>`],
+ ['contact','15. Questions and support',`<p>If you are unsure how a Pass, Advantage, listing or transaction works, read the relevant Docs before confirming the action. If an issue is specific to a Builder product or Advantage delivery, contact the Builder using the support information published for that Edition when available.</p><p>NexMarkets operator contact and formal legal entity details should be published with the production service before these Terms are treated as the final public legal notice. This page deliberately does not invent a company registration, address or governing-law jurisdiction that has not been supplied.</p>`]
+];
